    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline is a chain of small OfficeFloor function classes. To satisfy the spec \u2014 *on successful create, enqueue a welcome notification via the logger named `NOTIFY` carrying the owner id and memberId* \u2014 I followed the existing pattern rather than overloading any step:\n\n1. **New function class** `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java` \u2014 a single-responsibility step that logs one line on the `NOTIFY` logger with the owner id and `memberId`. It mirrors the existing `AuditOwnerCreated`/`EmitOwnerCreatedEvent` steps (which log to `AUDIT`), and sources the member id from `Owner.getPrimaryIdentifier()` \u2014 the same single accessor `OwnerCreatedEvent` uses, keeping the id consistent with the rest of the create side-effects.\n\n2. **Wired it into `owners.POST.yml`** as a new `enqueueWelcome` step, placed after `emitEvent` (so it runs after `SaveOwner` when the id and memberId are assigned) and before `resolveBulkWarning`, under the same `transaction` governance as its neighbours.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes \u2014 its `NOTIFY` capture confirms the line `Welcome owner: id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` contains both values \u2014 and nothing else regressed.",
